# Patch 0067 — Blank controls in the Privacy Center: Fluent message shapes
# must match the XUL element they land on (audit 2026-08-03; fixes strings
# from patches 0047-0050).
#
# XUL <menuitem> and <button> render their `label` ATTRIBUTE. A value-only
# Fluent message ("id = Text") sets textContent, which those elements never
# display — so the permission global-default selectors rendered three blank
# rows, the cookie-rule state menus rendered blank, and the Review/Hide/
# Clear all/Add-as-session-only buttons rendered blank. Conversely a XUL
# <label> renders its `value` attribute (or text children), so the two
# ".label =" messages aimed at labels displayed nothing either.
#
# 13 message-shape fixes, no markup or JS changes: the dynamic elements
# already go through document.l10n.setAttributes, which does the right
# thing once the message carries the right attribute. The codebase already
# knew this rule (kavacha-permissions-remove uses .label; patch 0054's ftl
# has a comment about it) — these were the stragglers.
diff --git a/locales/en-US/browser/browser/preferences/zen-preferences.ftl b/locales/en-US/browser/browser/preferences/zen-preferences.ftl
index 91d51a5..47bf90d 100644
